  "body_text": "96 \r\n A live test of training rights, licensing and payment. Media Trends Executive Preview \r\n Media Is Becoming AI’s First Major Test Case \n\n Media Trends Executive Preview Inside AI’s New Content Economy\n\n \r\n \r\n The fights unfolding across publishing and Hollywood could help determine how AI companies train models, license valuable material and compensate content owners far beyond the media industry.&nbsp; \n\n &nbsp; \n\n The new Media Trends Executive deep dive traces the legal decisions and emerging deals that could shape AI’s next phase. \n\n \r\n&nbsp;\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Unlock the full AI deep dive \r\n \r\n &#8202; Copyright without borders \n\n AI models can train on content legally in one country and deploy around the world, putting decades of copyright and fair-use precedent to the test.&nbsp;\n\n \r\n \r\n A new price for usage \n\n Retrieval-based agreements could tie publisher compensation more directly to how content is used, introducing a new model for negotiations between content owners and AI companies.&nbsp;\n\n \r\n \r\n Hollywood makes its first moves \n\n New studio agreements could help establish how companies use AI while protecting and monetizing valuable creative IP.\n\n \r\n &#8202; 🔐 \r\n&nbsp; Become a Media Trends Executive member to unlock the complete analysis, plus member-exclusive reporting on the forces reshaping media. &nbsp; \n\n &#8202; PO Box 101060 \n Arlington VA 22201 \n\n \r\n Contact Us \n Update Preferences \n\r\n Unsubscribe \n\n LinkedIn \n\n \r\n Facebook \n X \n\r\n Instagram \n\n PO Box 101060\nArlington VA 22201\n\n \r\n \r\n Contact Us \n Update Preferences \n\r\n Unsubscribe \n\n \r\n LinkedIn \n\n Facebook \n\r\n Twitter \n\n Instagram",
